 of ints) of length (s+1) ending at (r,c).\n    dp = [[[[] for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(k)]\n\n    # Base case: paths of length 1\n    for r in range(N):\n        for c in range(N):\n            dp[0][r][c] = [grid[r][c]]\n\n    # Neighbor directions: up, down, left, right.\n    dr = [-1, 1, 0, 0]\n    dc = [0, 0, -1, 1]\n\n    # Fill dp table for lengths 2..k\n    # s is the index for length s+1\n    for s in range(1, k):\n        for r in range(N):\n            for c in range(N):\n                current_val = grid[r][c]\n                # Initialize with a large sentinel list (values are in [1, N*N], so N*N+1 works).\n                sentinel = [N * N + 1] * (s + 1)\n                best = sentinel\n                for i in range(4):\n                    pr, pc = r + dr[i], c + dc[i]\n                    if 0 <= pr < N and 0 <= pc < N:\n                        prev_path = dp[s - 1][pr][pc]\n                        # prev_path should have length s\n                        if prev_path:\n                            candidate = prev_path + [current_val]\n                            if candidate < best:\n                                best = candidate\n                dp[s][r][c] = best\n\n    # Find the overall lexicographically smallest path among all end cells for length k\n    overall_best = [N * N + 1] * k\n    for r in range(N):\n        for c in range(N):\n            path = dp[k - 1][r][c]\n            if path and path < overall_best:\n                overall_best = path\n\n    return overall_best", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/129", "solution": "def minPath(grid, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the lexicographically minimal path of length k in an N x N grid\n    (each integer 1..N*N appears exactly once). You may start anywhere and\n    move each step to an orthogonally adjacent cell. Return the sequence of\n    values visited (length k). Assumes a uniqu