": "import math\ndef right_angle_triangle(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return True if the three\n    sides form a right-angled triangle, False otherwise.\n    A right-angled triangle is a triangle in which one angle is right angle or\n    90 degree.\n    Example:\n    right_angle_triangle(3, 4, 5) == True\n    right_angle_triangle(1, 2, 3) == False\n    '''\n    sides = sorted([a, b, c])\n    x, y, z = sides[0], sides[1], sides[2]\n\n    # Validate side lengths: must be positive and satisfy triangle inequality\n    if x <= 0 or y <= 0 or z <= 0:\n        return False\n    if x + y <= z:\n        return False\n\n    # Use isclose for float tolerance; default rel_tol and abs_tol are reasonable here\n    return math.isclose(x * x + y * y, z * z)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/157", "solution": "def right_angle_triangle(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return True if the three\n    sides form a right-angled triangle, False otherwise.\n    A right-angled triangle is a triangle in which one angle is right angle or\n    90 degree.\n    Example:\n    right_angle_triangle(3, 4, 5) == True\n    right_angle_triangle(1, 2, 3) == False\n    '''\n    import math\n    from numbers import Real\n\n    # Validate numeric input (reject booleans explicitly)\n    for name, val in (('a', a), ('b', b), ('c', c)):\n        if isinstance(val, bool) or not isinstance(val, Real):\n            return False\n        if not math.isfinite(val):\n            return False\n        if val <= 0:\n            return False\n\n    # Triangle inequality: sum of any two sides must be greater than the third\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return False\n\n    # Use sorted sides so the largest side is considered the hypotenuse\n    x, y, z = sorted((a, b, c))\n\n    # Use math.isclose to handle floating p